[2025-07-29 10:12:09.018] Group develop plan response: # TypeScript Compilation Error Fix Plan

## Summary
The errors indicate that TypeScript's iterator types have been updated to require a `[Symbol.dispose]` method, changing from `IterableIterator<T>` to `MapIterator<T>` and `SetIterator<T>`. This is likely due to TypeScript's support for the disposable pattern in newer versions.

## Root Cause Analysis
- The `DraftMap` and `DraftSet` classes extend native `Map` and `Set` types
- Their `keys()` methods return `IterableIterator<any>` but the base classes now expect `MapIterator<any>` and `SetIterator<any>` respectively
- The new iterator types include a `[Symbol.dispose]()` method for resource cleanup

## Fix Strategy
Update the return types of iterator methods in custom Map/Set implementations to use the new TypeScript iterator types that include the disposable symbol.

## Execution Plan

