    },
    {
      "pattern": "(class DraftSet[\\s\\S]*?)values\\(\\):\\s*IterableIterator<([^>]+)>",
      "replacement": "$1values(): SetIterator<$2>"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Expected Outcome
After applying these fixes, the TypeScript compiler should recognize that the iterator methods return the correct types (`MapIterator` and `SetIterator`) that include the required `[Symbol.dispose]` method, resolving the compilation errors.
